它应该用段落回答吗？
Should it respond in paragraphs?

509
00:41:56,078 --> 00:41:57,552
它应该用 JSON 回答吗？
Should it respond in JSON?

510
00:41:57,712 --> 00:41:59,792
它拥有什么样的数据边界，对吧？
What kind of data boundaries does it have, right?

511
00:41:59,952 --> 00:42:02,672
它应该如何使用它提供的信息？
How should it use the information that it has provided?

512
00:42:02,832 --> 00:42:14,512
我只想说，很多时候这取决于你实际连接到智能体的工具和知识，还有这个概念，
就是展示你的来源，说明用这个知识源来做某事，用这个工具来做某事，对吧？
I will just say, you know, a lot of times this has to do with what you actually connect to your agent, the tools and the knowledge,
but also this idea of you know, show your sources, talk about use this knowledge source for this and use this tool for this, right?

513
00:42:14,672 --> 00:42:25,152
这些不同的东西，你对它的质量期望，如果有人发送了一个它不一定知道如何回答的问题，
智能体应该如何处理错误或歧义，以及它该如何升级处理，对吧？
Those different things, quality expectations that you have for it, how the agent should handle errors or ambiguity if somebody sends a
question that it doesn't necessarily know how to answer, and as well as how does it escalate, right?

514
00:42:25,232 --> 00:42:26,672
这就是人机协同的概念。
This concept of human in the loop.

515
00:42:27,008 --> 00:42:29,648
我们也应该概述那些升级条件。
We should outline those escalation conditions as well.

516
00:42:29,888 --> 00:42:37,648
除了指令和模型，每个 AI 智能体还有三个组成部分，那就是知识、工具和其他智能体。
There's also outside of instructions and models three pieces of every AI agent, and that is knowledge, tools, and other agents.

517
00:42:37,870 --> 00:42:42,208
所以这里有一个关于什么是知识、什么是工具、什么是智能体的概念。
And so there's this concept around what is knowledge, what are tools, and what are agents.

518
00:42:42,368 --> 00:42:45,408
而知识实际上是我们锚定智能体的方式。
And knowledge really is the way we can ground our agents.

519
00:42:45,568 --> 00:42:47,088
我刚才已经说过好几次了，对吧？
I've said that a couple of times, right?

520
00:42:47,278 --> 00:42:48,768
人们经常使用那个术语。
People use that terminology a lot.

521
00:42:48,848 --> 00:42:51,808
但当我们思考如何锚定我们的智能体时，那意味着什么呢？
But when we think about grounding our agents, what does that mean?

522
00:42:51,968 --> 00:42:55,328
就是给预构建模型提供业务上下文。
It's giving it the business context with a pre-built model.

523
00:42:55,568 --> 00:43:00,048
工具是我们提供上下文给智能体，或者让智能体去执行任务的方式。
Tools is how we can either give our agent context or have our agent do things.

524
00:43:00,270 --> 00:43:06,448
所以我们谈论对话智能体与任务智能体，这些工具
就是我们将对话智能体转变为任务智能体的手段。
So we talk about chatting agents versus task agents, these tools is how we turn chatting agents into task agents.

525
00:43:06,608 --> 00:43:10,688
然后是智能体或智能体编排，我们稍后会详细讨论。
And then agents or agent orchestration, we're going to talk about more here in a little bit.

526
00:43:10,798 --> 00:43:16,688
但当我们谈到想要一个执行非常特定任务的智能体
时，假设我们有另一个执行非常特定任务的智能体。
But when we talk about we want an agent that does something very specific,
say we have another agent that does something else very specific.

527
00:43:16,846 --> 00:43:19,168
这里有一部分是这两个智能体应该互相交流。
And there's a part where these two agents should talk to each other.

528
00:43:19,248 --> 00:43:20,928
我们也有能力做到这一点。
We have the ability to do that as well.

529
00:43:21,102 --> 00:43:23,568
所以，实际上，这意味着什么时候需要知识？
And so, really, what this means, when do we need knowledge?

530
00:43:23,728 --> 00:43:25,808
当用户提问时，我们需要知识。
We need knowledge when a user asks a question.

531
00:43:25,968 --> 00:43:34,608
智能体随后会搜索它的知识源，无论是 PDF 文档、数据库，
还是 SharePoint 文件夹或 SharePoint 文档。
The agent then searches, you know, its knowledge source, whether it be a PDF document, whether it be a database,
whether it be a SharePoint folder or a SharePoint document.

532
00:43:34,768 --> 00:43:38,448
它会去检查那个知识源，然后在它的回答中使用它。
It goes and checks that knowledge source and then uses it in its response.

533
00:43:38,528 --> 00:43:42,608
它把这些信息带回给 LLM，以便它向用户提供回答。
It brings that back to the LLM to provide its response to the user.

534
00:43:42,768 --> 00:43:51,408
工具是指当我说明，嘿，我想更新一个案例，或者关闭一个案例，或者创建一个请假申请，
或者我想让你起草一封邮件，对吧？
Tools is when I say, Hey, I want to update a case or close a case or
create a time off request, or I want you to draft an email, right?

535
00:43:51,502 --> 00:43:58,208
不仅仅是在聊天中起草邮件，而是实际上连接到 Outlook，
让那封邮件草稿显示在那里，可以这么理解，对吧？
And not just draft an email in the chat, but actually connect to Outlook and have that email draft show up there, so to speak, right?

536
00:43:58,382 --> 00:44:00,688
就像是能够真正替我们去完成这些操作的能力。
Like the ability to go and actually do that for us.

537
00:44:00,910 --> 00:44:08,928
然后到智能体或智能体编排，这种能力是让每个智
能体都有非常特定的任务、非常特定的目的和范围。
And so then with agents or agent orchestration, this ability of we have
every agent have a very specific task, very specific purpose and scope.

538
00:44:09,038 --> 00:44:15,008
它可能需要与其它具有非常特定任务和范围的智能体交流，以帮助支持整个业务流程。
And it may need to talk to other very specific tasks and scoped agents to help support an entire business process.

539
00:44:15,182 --> 00:44:18,848
所以当我们谈论智能体知识时，具体是指什么呢？
So when we talk about agent knowledge, what does this mean in particular?

540
00:44:19,088 --> 00:44:22,848
这意味着我们拥有上下文数据集成。
What this means is we have contextual data integration.

541
00:44:23,008 --> 00:44:31,088
我们拥有可靠且负责任的 AI，也就是说知识锚定能让我们的 AI 输出符合组织政策，并减少幻觉。
We have reliable and responsible AI, as in grounding aligns our AI
outputs with our organizational policies and reduces the hallucinations.

542
00:44:31,248 --> 00:44:37,168
这些智能体就是我们的 LLM，我们的预构建模型实际上是按照我们组织的规范来响应的。
The agents are our LLMs, our pre-built models are actually responding in accordance with our organization.

543
00:44:37,328 --> 00:44:41,088
还有一个概念叫做 RAG，也就是检索增强生成。
And there's this concept called RAG, retrieval augmented generation.

544
00:44:41,168 --> 00:44:43,968
关于这个概念的具体表现，我把这张幻灯片放出来。
And really how this looks, I actually pulled in this slide.

545
00:44:44,048 --> 00:44:45,248
这是 Copilot，好吗。
This is copilot, all right.

546
00:44:45,328 --> 00:44:49,008
这是关于 M365 Copilot 如何工作的一些文档。
Some documentation on how M365 copilot works.

547
00:44:49,168 --> 00:44:52,688
你会看到这里有一个叫作知识锚定的概念。
And you'll see there's this concept called grounding here.

548
00:44:52,878 --> 00:44:54,768
就是这里的知识锚定，知识锚定。
This right here, grounding and grounding.

549
00:44:54,848 --> 00:44:55,648
我们在谈论什么？
What are we talking about?

550
00:44:55,808 --> 00:44:56,288
知识锚定。
Grounding.

551
00:44:56,448 --> 00:45:00,208
嗯，接下来发生的情况是，当人们进行对话时，就是上面这些人，对吧？
Well, what happens is, is when people chat, this is that people up here, right?

552
00:45:00,288 --> 00:45:05,728
他们使用 Copilot，顺着这个箭头看，然后到 2，它会进行知识锚定，连接到 Microsoft Graph。
And they use copilot, follow this one arrow, then it goes to two, it goes grounding to Microsoft Graph.

553
00:45:05,998 --> 00:45:13,248
它会获取你的电子邮件、文件、会议、聊天记录、录音、日历、联系人、OneDrive 文档、
SharePoint 文档，所有这些不同的内容。
This gets your emails, files, meetings, chats, recordings, calendars, contacts,
OneDrive documents, SharePoint documents, all of this different stuff.

554
00:45:13,328 --> 00:45:16,128
它会去检索并说：嘿，针对这个提示词，哪些内容与我相关？
It goes and says, Hey, regarding this prompt, what's relevant to me?

555
00:45:16,288 --> 00:45:22,448
然后它获取相关内容，并说：好，现在我们把这些内容发送给预构建大语言模型。
Then it gets what's relevant and it says, Okay, let's now actually send this over to the pre-built large language model.

556
00:45:22,606 --> 00:45:27,088
所以，预构建大语言模型实际接收到的是你的提示词加上任何知识锚定内容。
So, what the pre-built large language model is actually getting is your prompt plus any grounding.

557
00:45:27,182 --> 00:45:36,128
LLM 的响应不会直接返回给用户，它会返回进行后处理知识锚定，与你的信息进行比对，
以确保它是正确的，没有产生幻觉。
The LLM response doesn't just go back to the user, it goes back for a post-processing grounding to compare it back against your
information to make sure it's correct that it didn't hallucinate.

558
00:45:36,208 --> 00:45:39,248
最后，这就是发送回给用户的内容。
And then that is ultimately what is sent back to the user.

559
00:45:39,488 --> 00:45:42,848
这就是我们需要思考的知识锚定概念。
This is this concept of grounding that we need to think about.

560
00:45:43,008 --> 00:45:53,488
这就是知识的含义，也是为什么我们往往能——再次强调，在 99% 的情况下——通过知识锚定和知识，
让预构建模型了解我们的业务以及我们希望它做什么。
This is what knowledge is and why we can oftentimes, again, 99% of the time, have
pre-built models know our business and what we want it to do using grounding and knowledge.

561
00:45:53,648 --> 00:45:57,408
当我们谈论 RAG 时，RAG 有五个维度。
When we talk about RAG, there's kind of five dimensions to RAG.

562
00:45:57,582 --> 00:46:04,048
具体来说，Copilot 和 Copilot Studio 通过 Microsoft Graph 使用语义理解。
And so specifically, Copilot and Copilot Studio use semantic understanding through Microsoft Graph.

563
00:46:04,208 --> 00:46:07,968
那就是我刚才展示的那个信息图的底部角落。
That was that bottom corner of that infographic I just showed.

564
00:46:08,048 --> 00:46:17,248
这就是准确性的概念，也就是说，这个智能体现在发送给用户的内容，
是否真的反映了它在 Microsoft Graph 中找到的内容？
And so it's the idea of accuracy, as in hey, is what this agent now sending
to the user actually reflective of what it found in Microsoft Graph?

565
00:46:17,550 --> 00:46:23,952
这意味着相关性就像是：嘿，如果我问的是 X，它回答的是 X 还是回答的是 Y？
What this means is relevance is like, hey, if I asked about X, did it Respond about X or did it respond about Y?

566
00:46:24,192 --> 00:46:24,432
对吧。
Right.

567
00:46:24,512 --> 00:46:27,872
这个想法就是它返回的内容与我提问的内容是相关的。
This idea that like what it came back with was relevant to what I asked.

568
00:46:28,032 --> 00:46:30,112
及时性是指数据的时效性。
Timeliness is the freshness of the data.

569
00:46:30,272 --> 00:46:34,020
作为解决方案架构师，当我们谈论数据资产时，这一点非常重要。
This is really important as we talk about our data estate as a solution architect.

570
00:46:34,192 --> 00:46:38,592
理解就是让知识锚定在非 20 年前的资讯上，对吧？
Understanding is it grounding itself in information that's not 20 years old, right?

571
00:46:38,672 --> 00:46:43,952
但它是锚定在两年前或两个月前的资讯上，而不是 10 年前的资讯。
But it's grounding in the two-year-old information or the two-month-old information, not the 10-year-old information.

572
00:46:44,142 --> 00:46:53,072
整洁是指，你知道，我们的表格、CRM 或数据库是
去重过的，是准确的，而且具有代表性和可用性。
Cleanliness is, you know, the idea that our tables or our CRM or our databases are deduplicated, they're accurate,
and that they're representative and availability.

573
00:46:53,232 --> 00:46:59,072
作为架构师，Copilot 和智能体通常遵循用户的访问权限。
Copilot and agents generally, as an architect, generally abide by users' access level.

574
00:46:59,152 --> 00:47:01,392
所以我们也需要考虑这一点。
And so it's important for us to think about that as well.

575
00:47:01,632 --> 00:47:04,112
人们甚至能和这个系统交流吗？
Can people even talk to this system?

576
00:47:04,192 --> 00:47:04,432
对吧？
Right?

577
00:47:04,512 --> 00:47:07,232
那么他们可能就无法使用智能体代表他们去交流。
Then they might not be able to use an agent to talk to it on their behalf.

578
00:47:07,374 --> 00:47:09,632
所以这个概念是它对他们也是可用的。
And so this idea that it's also available to them.

579
00:47:09,870 --> 00:47:11,872
还有一个 RAG 流水线的概念。
There's also this concept of rag pipelines.

580
00:47:11,952 --> 00:47:15,552
在准备这次考试之前，我从未听说过 RAG 流水线。
I had never heard of a rag pipeline before preparing for this exam.

581
00:47:15,712 --> 00:47:31,072
RAG 流水线本质上就是关于如何摄入、流转、清洗、分块、嵌入、索引、检索、组装、
编排并监控所有智能体可访问数据的概念。
A rag pipeline is essentially this idea of how you ingest, stream, clean, chunk, embed, index, retrieve, assemble, orchestrate,
and monitor all of your data that agents can access.

582
00:47:31,312 --> 00:47:35,232
摄入就像是关于我们如何把那些信息带进来的概念。
Ingesting is like this idea of how we bring that information in.

583
00:47:35,566 --> 00:47:37,392
清洗，我觉得挺明显的，对吧？
Cleaning, I think, is pretty obvious, right?

584
00:47:37,472 --> 00:47:38,832
它是如何做到整洁的？
How is it uh cleanliness?

585
00:47:38,912 --> 00:47:39,792
它是如何保持最新的？
How is it up to date?

586
00:47:39,952 --> 00:47:44,592
分块、嵌入和索引其实就是关于它有多小、多易于处理的概念，对吧？
Chunking, and bedding and indexing is really this idea of how bite size is it, right?

587
00:47:44,718 --> 00:47:54,032
如果我们有一个巨大的 PDF 文档，假设它有 200 页长，Copilot 可能无法一次性理解所有内容。
If we have a massive PDF document, say it's 200 pages long, Copilot
probably won't be able to understand all of that content just in one pass.

588
00:47:54,192 --> 00:47:56,912
它需要把它分块处理，好，这一段是什么？
It needs to kind of chunk it up to understand, okay, what's this paragraph?

589
00:47:58,032 --> 00:47:58,912
现在，这一段又是什么？
Now, what's this paragraph?

590
00:47:59,072 --> 00:48:02,752
这第 100 段实际上就是我需要用来回答这个问题的段落。
This 100th paragraph is actually the paragraph that I need to respond to this question.

591
00:48:02,832 --> 00:48:05,952
这就是分块、索引以及所有相关环节的概念。
That's the idea of chunking and indexing and everything that goes into this.

592
00:48:06,032 --> 00:48:10,512
你不需要知道如何设置 RAG 流水线或它们如何工作的细节，但你只需要知道它们的存在。
You don't need to know how to set up rag pipelines or how they work in detail, but you really just need to know that they exist.

593
00:48:10,702 --> 00:48:17,316
这就是我们可以设置在系统中的自动化工具，可以帮助清理我们的智能体知识库。
This thing that we can set up in our system and automation that can help clean up our agentic knowledge bases.

594
00:48:17,552 --> 00:48:20,272
我们还有一个叫做生成式回答的概念。
We also have this concept called generative answers.

595
00:48:20,398 --> 00:48:22,672
这是 Copilot Studio 的一个概念。
And so this is a copilot studio concept.

596
00:48:22,830 --> 00:48:33,312
所以如果你想构建一个基于知识源并使用生成式编排的 Copilot Studio 智能体，
你就需要利用生成式回答来实现。
And so if you are wanting to build a copilot studio agent that uses generative orchestration based off of knowledge sources,
then you need to leverage generative answers in order to do that.

597
00:48:33,392 --> 00:48:38,992
如果你熟悉什么是主题，你可以在主题中使用生成式回答。
And so you can use generative answers inside of topics if you're familiar with what topics are.

598
00:48:39,182 --> 00:48:47,552
这意味着当用户询问关于某个主题的问题时，你的生成
式回答操作或节点会说：嘿，他们刚刚问了这个问题。
What this means is when a user asks a question about a certain topic, you have
your generative answers action or node say, Hey, they just asked about this.

599
00:48:47,792 --> 00:48:52,752
去查看这些特定的知识源，然后它会找到信息并回复用户。
Go look at these specific knowledge sources, and then it'll find the information and respond to the user.

600
00:48:52,974 --> 00:48:58,512
本质上，当你使用生成式回答时，你实际上是在回答「我们的内容里关于这个是怎么说的？」
Essentially, when you're using generative answers, you're effectively answering what does our content say about this?

601
00:48:58,672 --> 00:49:03,072
也就是说，这些知识源对于用户的提示词是怎么说的？
As in, what does these knowledge sources say about this user's prompt?

602
00:49:03,232 --> 00:49:07,312
在 Copilot Studio 中，特别是支持很多不同的知识源。
In Copilot Studio, there's a bunch of different supported knowledge sources in particular.

603
00:49:07,598 --> 00:49:11,712
Microsoft Learn 的考试内容涵盖了这些方面。
Microsoft Learn content for the exam covered these sort of things.

604
00:49:11,872 --> 00:49:16,832
我们可以有公共网站，也可以直接把文档上传到我们的智能体中。
We can have public websites, we can upload documents directly to our agent.

605
00:49:16,912 --> 00:49:24,512
当你上传这些时，如果你以前构建过 Copilot Studio 智能体，它实际上会获取这些信息，
将其分块，并在 Dataverse 中建立索引。
And when you upload that, if you've ever built a copilot studio agent, it
actually takes that information, chunks it, and indexes it inside of Dataverse.

606
00:49:24,672 --> 00:49:33,380
这意味着，从技术上讲，这就是你的智能体去获取信息的地方，说实话，
我之前并不太清楚这些信息是在哪里建立索引的。
And so what that means is that's actually where your agent is going and getting that information technically,
which I'll be honest was something I wasn't necessarily aware of or where that was indexed.

607
00:49:33,472 --> 00:49:37,312
但如果你上传过文档，有时它可能需要 10 分钟左右一直处于处理状态。
But if you've ever uploaded a document, sometimes it can take like 10 minutes and just sit there processing.

608
00:49:37,472 --> 00:49:41,872
原因是它正在为你的智能体进行分块和索引，以便智能体能够调用这些信息。
The reason is because it's chunking and indexing that information for your agent to be able to call on.

609
00:49:41,952 --> 00:49:47,792
我们可以添加 SharePoint 知识源，可以添加 Dataverse 表格，
也可以使用像 OneDrive 这样的企业级连接器。
We can add SharePoint knowledge sources, we can add Dataverse tables, we can also use enterprise connectors like OneDrive.

610
00:49:47,872 --> 00:49:51,472
我们还可以使用 Azure OpenAI 连接的数据和 Azure AI Search。
We can also use Azure OpenAI connected data and Azure AI Search.

611
00:49:51,566 --> 00:49:56,592
我们稍后会更多地讨论 Azure AI Search，但这里有一个限制。
And we're gonna talk about Azure AI Search more here in just a moment, but there is a limitation.

612
00:49:56,752 --> 00:50:00,912
一个智能体总共可以拥有 500 个知识源，这已经很多了。
You can have a total of 500 knowledge sources on an agent, which is a lot.

613
00:50:00,992 --> 00:50:04,032
我从未见过有人甚至接近需要用到这么多。
I've never seen anybody even come close to needing to use that.

614
00:50:04,272 --> 00:50:07,552
你只能拥有所谓的 5 个非结构化知识源。
You can only have what are called five unstructured knowledge sources.

