sure that it's our agent doesn't break or a business process doesn't fail, right?

1627
02:13:23,184 --> 02:13:29,984
我们如何确保，即使那是关键任务，我们也能处理那些超出我们控制范围的停机或返回的错误？
How do we make sure, even if that's a mission critical thing, that we're handling
those blackouts or errors that come back that might not be in our control?

1628
02:13:30,144 --> 02:13:32,064
行为与质量测试。
Behavioral and quality testing.

1629
02:13:32,270 --> 02:13:34,784
这就像是，嘿，我要求你做 X。
This is like, hey, I asked you to do X.

1630
02:13:34,944 --> 02:13:36,224
你是不是开始做 Y 了？
Did you start doing Y?

1631
02:13:36,544 --> 02:13:36,784
对吧？
Right?

1632
02:13:36,864 --> 02:13:38,224
或者你实际上是做了 X？
Or did you actually do X?

1633
02:13:38,384 --> 02:13:42,544
你做的内容是否准确，并且与我的问题或提示相关。
What you did was accurate and relevant to my question or my prompt.

1634
02:13:42,704 --> 02:13:46,624
对话质量很多时候是围绕，它是否连贯？
Conversation quality is a lot of times around like, is it coherent?

1635
02:13:46,784 --> 02:13:47,504
它是否流利？
Is it fluent?

1636
02:13:47,664 --> 02:13:49,824
比如，它是否在正确地使用我的语言？
Like, is it speaking my language correctly?

1637
02:13:50,062 --> 02:13:53,264
特别是如果我们使用小语言模型的话，它可能做不到。
Especially if we're using like small language models, maybe it might not.

1638
02:13:53,424 --> 02:13:59,184
现在很多大语言模型在连贯性、流利性等方面通常都没有问题。
A lot of the large language models generally have no problem today with coherence and fluency and those sort of things.

1639
02:13:59,278 --> 02:14:00,944
但我们的知识覆盖率怎么样？
But what kind of knowledge coverage do we have?

1640
02:14:01,104 --> 02:14:01,824
或者我们漏掉了什么？
Or are we missing?

1641
02:14:01,934 --> 02:14:08,064
比如，我是不是在问某些这个智能体应该处理的主题，
但它实际上并没有相关的知识源来支持这项工作？
Like, is it am I asking about a certain topic that this agent should handle
that it doesn't actually have a knowledge source to support that work?

1642
02:14:08,238 --> 02:14:10,784
可能还包括语气和输出格式。
Maybe the tone and as well as the output format.

1643
02:14:10,864 --> 02:14:15,424
它应该以段落、项目符号、表格、JSON，还是是/否的布尔值来输出？
Should it be outputting in paragraphs, bullet points, tables, JSON, yes and no Booleans?

1644
02:14:15,504 --> 02:14:16,544
也就是说，它应该怎么输出？
Like, how should it be outputting?

1645
02:14:16,718 --> 02:14:17,744
安全和合规。
Safety and compliance.

1646
02:14:17,838 --> 02:14:19,664
我觉得这部分是显而易见的，对吧？
I think this is self-explanatory, right?

1647
02:14:19,758 --> 02:14:25,744
护栏在检查有害内容、敏感数据保护、安全和合规要求方面的效果如何？
How effective are the guardrails at checking harmful content, sensitive data protection, security and compliance requirements?

1648
02:14:25,904 --> 02:14:26,944
然后是可用性测试。
then usability testing.

1649
02:14:27,024 --> 02:14:31,024
这非常类似于基于场景的测试，但这是在测它的可用性如何？
This is very similar to scenario-based testing, but this is how usable is it?

1650
02:14:31,184 --> 02:14:33,184
用户的满意度如何，对吧？
What's the user satisfaction, right?

1651
02:14:33,264 --> 02:14:36,864
他们是给它打一星还是五星？
Do they rank it a one out of five stars or a five out of five stars?

1652
02:14:37,024 --> 02:14:39,104
我们有哪些反馈循环，对吧？
What kind of feedback loops do we have, right?

1653
02:14:39,424 --> 02:14:41,504
我们可以对问题点赞或点踩。
We can thumbs up or thumbs down questions.

1654
02:14:41,678 --> 02:14:44,784
还有常规的调查，我们会要求人们提交反馈。
There's regular surveys where we ask people to submit their feedback.

1655
02:14:44,944 --> 02:14:47,424
实际任务完成的频率是多少？
How common is an actual task being completed?

1656
02:14:47,584 --> 02:14:51,984
如果有人说，嘿，我想起草一封邮件，邮件实际上被起草的频率是多少？
If somebody says, hey, I want to draft an email, how often is an email actually getting drafted?

1657
02:14:52,144 --> 02:14:55,344
所有这些内容都会纳入这些指标中。
All of those sort of things go into those sort of metrics.

1658
02:14:55,598 --> 02:14:57,700
所以这些都是测试范围的一部分，对吧？
So this is all kind of a part of testing scope, right?

1659
02:14:57,904 --> 02:14:58,864
我们要测试什么？
What are we testing?

1660
02:14:58,944 --> 02:15:02,464
但正如我们所知，测试用例的另一部分是测试数据。
But as we know, the other part of test cases are testing data.

1661
02:15:02,606 --> 02:15:04,304
实际上有两种不同类型的数据集。
There's actually two different types of data sets.

1662
02:15:04,464 --> 02:15:08,464
在参加这次考试之前，我甚至还不熟悉这两个不同的术语。
And before this exam, I wasn't even familiar with these two different terminologies.

1663
02:15:08,544 --> 02:15:09,984
所以这对你来说很重要。
So it's important for you to know.

1664
02:15:10,144 --> 02:15:14,224
基本上，我们显然知道，如果我们想做好测试，就需要不同类型的数据。
And essentially, we obviously know if we're going to test well, we need different types of data.

1665
02:15:14,384 --> 02:15:15,504
我们需要准确的数据。
We need accurate data.

1666
02:15:15,598 --> 02:15:18,784
所以你需要了解不同类型的数据集。
And so there's different different types of data sets you need to be aware of.

1667
02:15:18,944 --> 02:15:22,304
红数据集是可变且用于实验的内容。
A red data set is something that is mutable and experimental.

1668
02:15:22,464 --> 02:15:27,904
本质上，这意味着这是用于开发、测试和实验的。
Essentially, what that means is this is like the the development or testing and experimentation.

1669
02:15:28,110 --> 02:15:36,624
所以这可能并不一定是一个能够代表你所有账户、联系人或潜在客户之类的完整数据集。
So this might not necessarily have like this might not be a data set that might be like super representative of, say,
all of your accounts or your contacts or your leads or something like that.

1670
02:15:36,784 --> 02:15:40,704
但它的特点是灵活且可变的。
But what this is is, you know, this is something that is flexible and changeable.

1671
02:15:40,784 --> 02:15:43,184
它不被批准用于生产环境的决策。
It's not approved for production decision making.

1672
02:15:43,344 --> 02:15:46,144
它可能包含不断演变的数据架构，诸如此类的事情。
It may contain evolving schemas, you know, things like that.

1673
02:15:46,224 --> 02:15:48,944
它是我们的原型，是我们的红数据集。
It's a it's our prototyping, it's our red data set.

1674
02:15:49,038 --> 02:15:55,488
相比之下，金数据集就像是作为事实来源的冻结数据集。
Whereas opposed to our gold data sets, what these are are like Frozen data sets as a source of truth.

1675
02:15:55,662 --> 02:15:59,888
例如，当我们谈到智能体生命周期时，有一个暂存步骤。
So, for example, when we talked about the agent lifecycle, there was a staging step.

1676
02:16:00,048 --> 02:16:05,488
在生产环境之前的这个暂存步骤，就是我们首先用金数据集来测试智能体的地方。
This staging step before production is where we can first test our agent against a gold data set.

1677
02:16:05,568 --> 02:16:10,448
这可能表现为将生产数据复制到 UAT 环境中。
What this may look like is a copy of the production data into the UAT environment.

1678
02:16:10,528 --> 02:16:13,968
然后我们利用智能体与生产数据的副本进行交互。
And then we leverage our agent talking to the copy of the production data.

1679
02:16:14,048 --> 02:16:15,648
所以这不一定就是这个，对吧？
So it's not necessarily this, right?

1680
02:16:15,728 --> 02:16:22,608
这里是实验性的，可能不具代表性，可能不是全集，但这就是所谓的生产数据。
Where this is experimental, might not be representative, it might not
be a full set, but this is actually like production data, so to speak.

1681
02:16:22,688 --> 02:16:24,848
但我们不一定能去改动它，因为它被冻结了。
But we're not necessarily able to, you know, it's frozen.

1682
02:16:24,928 --> 02:16:30,928
我们不一定想更改生产数据，但我们想用它来进行测试、基准测试和部署。
We're not necessarily trying to change production data, but we're trying to use it for testing, benchmarking, and deployment.

1683
02:16:31,150 --> 02:16:36,448
所以这个概念是，如果你想把红数据集理解为可以随意玩弄、实验的，没问题。
So this idea, you know, if we if we wanted to think about red being play around with it, experimental, no problem.

1684
02:16:36,608 --> 02:16:39,008
金数据集就是所谓的金标准，对吧？
Gold, it's the gold standard, so to speak, right?

1685
02:16:39,150 --> 02:16:40,448
它是生产数据。
It's the production data.

1686
02:16:40,608 --> 02:16:43,968
这就是我们可以看到的两种不同类型的数据集。
This is the thing, the the two different types of data sets we could look at.

1687
02:16:44,128 --> 02:16:47,168
现在是时候谈谈智能体监控了。
It's now time we talk about agent monitoring.

1688
02:16:47,248 --> 02:16:51,647
这是我们今天的倒数第二个子话题。
And this is our second to last subtopic for today.

1689
02:16:51,918 --> 02:16:53,168
所以我们快讲完了。
So we we are almost there.

1690
02:16:53,326 --> 02:16:55,727
当我们谈论智能体监控时，对吧？
As we talk about agent monitoring, right?

1691
02:16:55,852 --> 02:17:02,048
我觉得讨论或头脑风暴它的含义很容易，但让我们从非常实际的角度来谈谈这意味着什么。
I think it's easy to discuss or to kind of brainstorm what this means, but let's talk about it very practically what this means.

1692
02:17:02,222 --> 02:17:03,888
有几个关键指标。
There are a couple of key metrics.

1693
02:17:04,076 --> 02:17:13,008
很多时候，这些指标可以与那些测试指标联系起来，顺便提一下，
我们应该在智能体运行过程中一直监控这些指标，对吧？
A lot of times these can be tied to the same as those testing metrics, side note,
that we should be monitoring throughout the operations of our agents, right?

1694
02:17:13,088 --> 02:17:14,688
第一个是运行健康状况。
And the first one being operational health.

1695
02:17:14,768 --> 02:17:16,528
这是最通用、最广泛的。
This is kind of the most general and broad.

1696
02:17:16,688 --> 02:17:27,168
我们要确保没有错误率或故障，确保有弹性，看看在智能体无法解决问题并升级到人工处理方面
有哪些升级趋势，诸如此类的事情。
We want to make sure there's no error rates or failures, that there's resiliency,
what kind of escalation trends are there in terms of an agent can't figure it out, so it escalates to a human, those sort of things.

1697
02:17:27,374 --> 02:17:28,768
我们还有性能指标。
We have performance metrics.

1698
02:17:28,848 --> 02:17:30,928
所以这些和性能测试完全一样。
So these are exactly the same as the performance test.

1699
02:17:31,054 --> 02:17:34,768
我们正在测试它的响应速度、吞吐量以及成功率。
We're testing how quickly it responds, what its throughput is, what its success rate is.

1700
02:17:35,008 --> 02:17:36,128
资源利用率。
Resource utilization.

1701
02:17:36,288 --> 02:17:41,888
这基本上就是，嘿，如果我们把它连接到一堆工具，但它只用其中一个，那为什么？
This essentially, hey, if we've connected it to a bunch of tools, but it only uses like one of the tools, why?

1702
02:17:42,062 --> 02:17:44,608
为什么它只利用其中一个资源？
Why is it only utilizing one of those resources?

1703
02:17:44,768 --> 02:17:49,218
如果它同时使用多个资源，会不会更高效？还有模型漂移的问题。
Would it be more efficient if it used multiple of those resources as well as that model drift?

1704
02:17:49,406 --> 02:17:56,768
质量和输出准确性就是响应准确性，这又是这样一个概念：如果我问关于 X 的问题，
它是否回答了关于 X 的内容，对吧？
Quality and output accuracy is the response accuracy, is again this concept that if I asked about X, did it respond about X, right?

1705
02:17:56,848 --> 02:17:57,727
还是它回答了关于 Y 的内容？
Or did it respond about Y?

1706
02:17:57,968 --> 02:17:59,326
它是不是开始聊别的事情了？
Did it start talking about something else?

1707
02:17:59,438 --> 02:18:03,326
或者它给出了关于 X 的错误答案，对吧？
Or did it come back and say an incorrect answer about X, right?

1708
02:18:03,486 --> 02:18:04,208
就是这个想法。
That idea.

1709
02:18:04,368 --> 02:18:07,647
知识覆盖率与这种资源利用率非常相似。
Knowledge coverage is very similar to this resource utilization.

1710
02:18:07,808 --> 02:18:18,048
这个想法是，我们是否拥有智能体需要访问的所有知识，它是否能访问这些内容，
还有它的行动有效性、输出完整性和相关性。
This idea that we have all of the knowledge that we need our agent to have access to, that it has access to those things,
its action effectiveness and its output completeness and relevance.

1711
02:18:18,208 --> 02:18:21,956
使用亮点主要围绕有多少活跃用户，有多少对话正在进行？
Usage highlights is around how many active users, how many conversations are happening?

1712
02:18:22,128 --> 02:18:27,168
我们的智能体最常调用哪些工具，或者检索哪些知识源？
What are the most common tools that are being called or knowledge sources that are being retrieved by our agents?

1713
02:18:27,342 --> 02:18:30,448
我们的 Copilot Studio 智能体最常触发哪些主题？
What are the most common topics for our copilot Studio agents that are being triggered?

1714
02:18:30,670 --> 02:18:33,088
我们的智能体中哪些功能被利用最多？
What sort of features in our agents are being utilized the most?

1715
02:18:33,262 --> 02:18:34,724
哪些功能又没被利用？
And which ones are not being utilized?

1716
02:18:34,928 --> 02:18:37,326
哪些部门在采用我们的智能体？
What sort of departments are adopting our agents?

1717
02:18:37,486 --> 02:18:39,168
哪些人群在采用我们的智能体？
What sort of people are adopting our agents?

1718
02:18:39,308 --> 02:18:42,048
哪些部门或人群没有采用我们的智能体？
What sort of departments or people are not adopting our agents?

1719
02:18:42,208 --> 02:18:44,928
所有这些关于使用情况的东西，也就是用户体验。
All of that sort of usage stuff, user experience.

1720
02:18:45,038 --> 02:18:48,928
同样，这些都是基于那些使用测试能力。
Again, this is based off of that uh that usage testing capabilities.

1721
02:18:49,102 --> 02:18:52,208
有多少次任务是完成了，有多少次是实际上被放弃了？
How many times are tasks being completed versus actually being abandoned?

1722
02:18:52,288 --> 02:18:54,448
有多少次是转交给人工处理的？
How many times are they being escalated to a human?

1723
02:18:54,638 --> 02:18:56,368
我们的 CSAT 分数是多少，对吧？
What are our CSAT scores, right?

1724
02:18:56,448 --> 02:18:58,768
我们的用户满意度分数是多少？
Are our user satisfied use scores?

1725
02:18:58,894 --> 02:19:01,888
有多少次用户点赞或点踩了一条消息？
How many times are people liking or disliking a message?

1726
02:19:02,208 --> 02:19:04,688
我们拿到的是五星、三星还是一星？
are we getting five stars, three stars, or one stars?

1727
02:19:04,848 --> 02:19:07,168
各种调查或反馈的趋势。
All sorts of survey or feedback sort of trends.

1728
02:19:07,248 --> 02:19:10,128
然后我们还有任何方面的风险、合规和安全问题。
And then also we have any kind of risk compliance and security.

1729
02:19:10,288 --> 02:19:15,647
这里有很多不同的工具可以用来追踪我稍后要展示的这些内容。
There's all sorts of different tools to be able to track these different things that I'm going to showcase here in just a moment.

1730
02:19:15,808 --> 02:19:20,448
不过在开始之前，我还想强调一下 AI 故障排除的步骤。
I also wanted to highlight though, before we do that, an AI troubleshooting step.

1731
02:19:20,528 --> 02:19:20,768
好的。
All right.

1732
02:19:20,878 --> 02:19:23,486
所以再次强调，作为架构师，你是一个规划者。
So again, if we think about as an architect, you're you're a map.

1733
02:19:24,110 --> 02:19:24,528
对吧？
person, right?

1734
02:19:24,608 --> 02:19:25,636
你是个设计人员。
You're a design person.

1735
02:19:25,727 --> 02:19:27,075
你是个制定蓝图的人。
You're a blueprinting person.

1736
02:19:27,168 --> 02:19:31,808
你需要能够思考，比如，如果我们遇到某种问题，可能的成因是什么？
You need to be able to think about like, hey, if we're having some kind of issue, what is the likely cause?

1737
02:19:32,013 --> 02:19:35,459
比如我们如何映射到，我们如何故障排除那个问题？
Like how do we map to a how do we troubleshoot that thing?

1738
02:19:35,566 --> 02:19:37,968
我们如何将问题映射到解决方案上？
How do we map an issue to a resolution?

1739
02:19:38,156 --> 02:19:43,248
所以我有点想强调一下，读一些我从 Microsoft Learn 文档中获取的内容。
And so I kind of wanted to just highlight some of these, read some of these that I took from the Microsoft Learn documentation.

1740
02:19:43,406 --> 02:19:46,848
比如如果我们遇到模型或提示词问题，那可能意味着什么？
Where say we're having a model or a prompt issue, what could that mean?

1741
02:19:47,084 --> 02:19:50,528
也许意味着我们的指令很差，或者人们发送了模糊的提示词。
Maybe it means we have poor instructions or people are sending unclear prompts.

1742
02:19:50,734 --> 02:19:52,128
假设我们存在知识差距，对吧？
Say we have knowledge gaps, right?

1743
02:19:52,368 --> 02:19:55,168
它给出了错误的回答，比如这就不对。
It's giving an incorrect response like this is not right.

1744
02:19:55,374 --> 02:20:01,008
所有可能的成因包括知识差距，这意味着它可能缺少、过时或不完整的基准数据。
All the likely causes a knowledge gap, which means it could be having missing, outdated or incomplete grounding data.

1745
02:20:01,168 --> 02:20:04,848
有一个知识源我们需要更新、移除或添加到我们的智能体中。
There's a knowledge source we need to update or remove or add to our agent.

1746
02:20:05,102 --> 02:20:06,848
假设我们有集成故障，对吧？
Say we have integration failures, right?

1747
02:20:06,928 --> 02:20:11,248
我们正在连接这个第三方智能体，连接这个第三方服务，但它没起作用。
We're connecting to this third party agent, we're connecting to this third party service and it's not working.

1748
02:20:11,408 --> 02:20:24,448
我们需要弄清楚原因，比如我们频繁重启或失败，或者我们的审计日志显示我们的 CSAT 大幅下
降，因为它开始回答说我不知道怎么回答，因为集成失败了。
We need to understand why that is as in say we're having frequent restarts or failures or you know our audit logs seem to be you know
our our CSAT has gone down tremendously because it starts responding I don't know how to answer that because a integration is failing.

1749
02:20:24,608 --> 02:20:27,088
假设我们有更多配置类型的问题。
Say we have more like configuration type issues.

1750
02:20:27,248 --> 02:20:31,328
这将涉及权限、角色、环境变量之类的东西。
This is going to be around permissions, roles, environment variables, stuff like that.

1751
